acceptance_criteria:
measured timeout/queue/spool limits; no unbounded retries/timers;
accepted events eventually arrive once under the defined idempotency contract;
dropped events are classified; shutdown/reload neither hangs nor leaves active
handlers. Offline capture remains best-effort without claiming full transcripts.

actual pinned client with hooks-only, MCP-only, and both installed;
stable tool names/count and exactly one intended request per invocation;
no shadowed tools, silent broadening of enabled tools, duplicate registration,
double capture or uncontrolled memory-tool-result feedback. Reinstall and
startup order do not change authority. Native settings retain runtime
`bearerTokenEnvVar`, not literal secrets; test absence/rotation of that variable.
